SwiftPutty local patch 0002
Upstream: PuTTY 0.85 (a3cce3a48d4ab12e0fccb32998b9042d4f7c3ff1)
Status:   not yet reported upstream; suitable for upstreaming

pollwrap.c: report POLLHUP to an fd waiting for writability.

uxsel's model is select(): a socket waiting for SELECT_W is reported
writable when it has a pending error or the connection is gone, and the
backend then discovers the error (e.g. via SO_ERROR after a non-blocking
connect()). pollwrap translated that to poll(), but only POLLOUT and
POLLERR counted as "writable".

On macOS, poll() reports a refused non-blocking connect() on a TCP socket
as POLLHUP alone (no POLLOUT, no POLLERR), while select() marks the same
socket writable. pollwrap_get_fd_rwx() therefore returned 0 for the
socket, nothing was dispatched, and every later poll() returned at once:
the event loop spun at 100% CPU and the connection never reported its
failure. unix/cliloop.c (plink, psftp, pscp) and SwiftPutty's core loop
are both affected.

Count POLLHUP as writable too, as already done for readability, which
matches select().

--- a/unix/utils/pollwrap.c
+++ b/unix/utils/pollwrap.c
@@ -116,7 +116,7 @@
 #define SELECT_X_IN (POLLPRI)
 
 #define SELECT_R_OUT (SELECT_R_IN | POLLERR | POLLHUP)
-#define SELECT_W_OUT (SELECT_W_IN | POLLERR)
+#define SELECT_W_OUT (SELECT_W_IN | POLLERR | POLLHUP)
 #define SELECT_X_OUT (SELECT_X_IN)
 
 void pollwrap_add_fd_rwx(pollwrapper *pw, int fd, int rwx)
